  "id": "DrugBank_DB00153 - MONDO_24298",
  "verbalization": "Ergocalciferol, also known as vitamin D3, is implicated in the pathogenesis of Vitamin Deficiency Disorder through a series of interconnected indications. The evidence suggests that Ergocalciferol is linked to Rickets and Osteomalacia, both of which are conditions associated with vitamin D deficiency and its metabolic consequences. These diseases are mediated through the induction of Cholecalciferol, a form of vitamin D, which in turn is linked to the Vitamin Deficiency Disorder. The overlapping pathways highlight a potential mechanism by which Ergocalciferol may influence vitamin D metabolism, thereby contributing to the development of the disorder. The consistent presence of Cholecalciferol as a mediator across different indications supports the hypothesis that Ergocalciferol plays a role in the regulation of vitamin D levels, which could be relevant in the context of vitamin deficiency. The evidence underscores a functional relationship between Ergocalciferol and the vitamin deficiency disorder, emphasizing the importance of vitamin D metabolism in the pathophysiology of the condition.",
